<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Picardy</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Picardy is a historical region of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, centred on the Somme valley, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amiens">Amiens</a> as its main city and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beauvais">Beauvais</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-quentin">Saint-Quentin</a> among its towns. A French province under the old regime, it was an administrative region from the 1960s until 2016, when it merged with Nord-Pas-de-Calais into Hauts-de-France. Its open farmland was a frequent battleground, notably in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-somme">Battle of the Somme</a> in 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/picardy.jpg" alt="Picardy" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Patricia.fidi · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Picardie.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
